; expect 40
; The FLOOR under `expMaxDecls`, and the reason it is a file rather
; than a number in a comment.
;
; `expand.ax`'s budget on phase-D output is 10,000 declarations, set
; against a measured ceiling: the whole self-hosted compiler is 2,535
; symbols and `stdlib/` and `self_host/` declare no declaration macros
; at all, so nothing in this repository comes near it. That is exactly
; the condition under which a floor rots - a limit no real code
; approaches can be lowered into real code without anything going red,
; and this repository has already recorded that lesson twice about
; numbers in gates.
;
; So this generates a few hundred declarations on purpose. `pair` runs
; a declaration-position `syntax/for` over a 40-constructor type and
; emits a signature and a function for each, which is 80 generated
; declarations from one invocation - legal, ordinary, and the shape a
; real `derive` grows into. Lowering the budget under it turns this
; case red instead of turning a user's program into a refusal.
;
; The probe sums nothing clever: `main` calls the generated function
; for the last constructor, so the case fails if the iteration stops
; early as well as if the budget refuses it.
(data Wide
  (K0)
  (K1)
  (K2)
  (K3)
  (K4)
  (K5)
  (K6)
  (K7)
  (K8)
  (K9)
  (K10)
  (K11)
  (K12)
  (K13)
  (K14)
  (K15)
  (K16)
  (K17)
  (K18)
  (K19)
  (K20)
  (K21)
  (K22)
  (K23)
  (K24)
  (K25)
  (K26)
  (K27)
  (K28)
  (K29)
  (K30)
  (K31)
  (K32)
  (K33)
  (K34)
  (K35)
  (K36)
  (K37)
  (K38)
  (K39))

(macro pair ((pair T)
   (syntax/for (C (syntax/constructors T))
     (:: (syntax/join idx C) (-> T Int))
     (fn ((syntax/join idx C) v) 40))))

(pair Wide)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (idxK39 K39))
